{"term":"landlord","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a3e699aecaa5c912d3","definition":"A person that leases real property; a lessor.","example":"Brethren, brethren, it were better to haue this communitie,\nThen to haue this difference in degrees:\nThe landlord his rent, the lawyer his fees.\nSo quickly the poore mans ſubſtance is ſpent […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["lessor","lease provider","leaser"],"antonyms":["tenant","lessee"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["head landlord","landchad","landlording","landlordish","landlordism","landlordless","landlordly","landlordry","landlordship","landlord special","nonlandlord","Randlord","slumlord","social landlord","sub-landlord","superior landlord"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landlord#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6023c6cc3349dbf028","definition":"The owner or manager of a public house.","example":"When asked to explain why he became a landlord, he told the Archbishop of York it was so he could close the pub on Sundays, and suppress the profane language and singing that came through the bar windows.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["publican"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK","register":"UK","wordFamily":["head landlord","landchad","landlording","landlordish","landlordism","landlordless","landlordly","landlordry","landlordship","landlord special","nonlandlord","Randlord","slumlord","social landlord","sub-landlord","superior landlord"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landlord#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:01512ece21828a36f0","definition":"A shark, imagined as the owner of the surf to be avoided.","example":"the lurking presence of “The Landlord”","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang, with-definite-article","register":"slang, with-definite-article","wordFamily":["head landlord","landchad","landlording","landlordish","landlordism","landlordless","landlordly","landlordry","landlordship","landlord special","nonlandlord","Randlord","slumlord","social landlord","sub-landlord","superior landlord"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landlord#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e38b1c12e682ea9aea","definition":"To lease real property; to act as a lessor.","example":"All kinds of \"Dulishevskis\" were \"landlording\" in Tisza's time, and have continued under the Communists.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"rare","register":"rare, transitive","wordFamily":["head landlord","landchad","landlording","landlordish","landlordism","landlordless","landlordly","landlordry","landlordship","landlord special","nonlandlord","Randlord","slumlord","social landlord","sub-landlord","superior landlord"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/landlord#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈlænd.lɔːd/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/44/En-au-landlord.ogg/En-au-landlord.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["head landlord","landchad","landlording","landlordish","landlordism","landlordless","landlordly","landlordry","landlordship","landlord special","nonlandlord","Randlord","slumlord","social landlord","sub-landlord","superior landlord"]}